    Hosted: `GET /health` → `{"ok":true,"db":"up"}`. `GET /ready` → `authOrigin: true`, `signupOpen: false`. Then the synthetic operator journey on throwaway data only.
    
    ## ROLL BACK
    
    Local: stop the app, restore the last physical backup (`pg-backup.mjs restore <tar> --replace-live-data`), check out the previous SHA, start Postgres + migrate + app, confirm `/health` and a sign-in.
    
    Hosted: redeploy the previous candidate SHA. Use Neon PITR if data must move back. Do **not** disable TLS, auth, tenant checks, or signup closure.
    
    ## DATABASE BACKUP
    
    Local: `npm run test:backup` proves the isolated path. Operator backup: `node scripts/pg-backup.mjs backup`. Archives are not customer exports.
    
    Hosted: configure Neon PITR / backups on the Neon side. Application tar backup is for the local cluster only.
    
    ## DATABASE RESTORE
    
    `node scripts/pg-backup.mjs restore <archive.tar.gz> --replace-live-data`  
    Without the flag the CLI exits 2 (will not overwrite live `data/postgres`). Prove on the isolated port first.
    
    ## FAILED MIGRATION
    
    `scripts/migrate.mjs` applies each file in one transaction and records `_migrations`. A failed file rolls back; retry is safe. Do not edit an already-applied file — add a new `00xx_*.sql`. If 0009/0010 archive orphan facts, that is intentional (dangling/cross-org sources cannot stay GREEN). They do not delete fact rows.
    
    ## AUTH FAILURE
    
    - LAN IP over HTTP will not keep `__Host-` cookies. Use `localhost` or HTTPS.
    - Hosted sessions bounce: `BETTER_AUTH_URL` does not match the browser origin.
    - `/ready` `"authOrigin": false`: HTTPS origin missing.
    - Rotate `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` only with a planned sign-out of every session.
    
    ## DATABASE OUTAGE
    
    Symptoms: `/health` 503, UI “Database unavailable”, scrubbed `[db] pool error` logs.
    
    1. Local: `node scripts/pg-local.mjs status` then `start` then `npm run db:migrate`.
    2. Hosted: check Neon status. Do not set `sslmode=disable`.
    3. Confirm `/health` 200 before sending operators back.
    
    ## COMPROMISED SECRET
    
    1. Rotate the affected secret (`BETTER_AUTH_SECRET`, `DATABASE_URL` password, `XAI_API_KEY`, invite codes).
    2. Do not commit the new value. Do not paste it into chat.
    3. Re-invite members (old invite ids die). Audit for unexpected memberships.
    4. Record the incident; do not claim the leak never happened.
    
    ## TENANT-ISOLATION INCIDENT
    
    1. Do not relax tests.
    2. `npm run test:live-idor` against the running app.
    3. `node scripts/mutation-isolation.mjs`
    4. If confirmed: take the origin off the network, preserve logs, notify Andrew.
    
